import lib/process.dl

function the descendant process test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set setup to a process command for the descendant process test interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to setup
add "import os; os.remove('descendant-finished.tmp') if os.path.exists('descendant-finished.tmp') else None" as an argument to setup
use "tests/required/process_descendant_output" as the working directory of setup
run setup and set preparation to it

set command to a process command for the descendant process test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import subprocess,sys,time\ncode=\"import os\\nchunk=b'D'*4096\\ntry:\\n while True:\\n  os.write(1,chunk)\\n  os.write(2,chunk)\\nexcept OSError:\\n open('descendant-finished.tmp','w').close()\"\nsubprocess.Popen([sys.executable,'-c',code])\ntime.sleep(0.1)" as an argument to command
use "tests/required/process_descendant_output" as the working directory of command
launch command and set child to it

wait for child and set status to it
read the available standard output of child and set output to it
read the available standard error of child and set error to it
clean up child and set cleanup to it

set verification to a process command for the descendant process test interpreter
add "-c" as an argument to verification
add "import os,time; time.sleep(1); finished=os.path.exists('descendant-finished.tmp'); print(finished); os.remove('descendant-finished.tmp') if finished else None" as an argument to verification
use "tests/required/process_descendant_output" as the working directory of verification
run verification and set check to it

print whether preparation succeeded as a line
print whether child was launched as a line
print whether status succeeded as a line
print whether status reports completion as a line
print whether output succeeded as a line
print whether (output's contents's length > 0) as a line
print whether error succeeded as a line
print whether (error's contents's length > 0) as a line
print whether cleanup succeeded as a line
print whether check succeeded as a line
print whether (check's standard output = "True\n") as a line
